{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1189230-the-salinian-working-in-mage-the-awakening-signs-of-sorcery-preview-materials","id":1189230,"title":"The Salinian working in Mage the Awakening [Signs of Sorcery preview materials]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-24T08:15:30-08:00","id":1189230,"title":"The Salinian working in Mage the Awakening [Signs of Sorcery preview materials]","content":"So i was reading some Exalted stuff, and came across the Salinian working, which for those who aren't that familiar with Exalted, this is a ritual that inscribed caches of sorcerous knowledge into creation.<br /> At first, this screamed out Archmasters and Archmagic...<br /> But then i remembered the Signs of Sorcery preview had some interesting stuff on Grimoires and Daimonomikons...<br /> <br /> Namely this:<br /> <br /> <b>Astral Grimoire (Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022 + Prime \u2022)</b><br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Cost: 1 Mana<br /> Withstand: Total Arcanum dots used in the rote<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Expression, Occult<br /> Scribing an Astral Grimoire is much like scribing an earthly one, except the vessel which holds the symbols exists only in the subject's Oneiros. An Awakened subject can cast the rotes from the<br /> Grimoire without having to meditate into the Astral, but if she does cast with the Astral representation of the Grimoire in hand, it grants a two-die Equipment bonus to all casting rolls.<br /> Summoning the Goetia that represents the Grimoire has the same effect. <br /> +1 Reach: The mage can scribe a Grimoire into the Temenos, making it available to anyone who travels there. The rotes can only be cast directly from the Astral representation or with its<br /> summoned Goetia, neither of which grants an Equipment bonus.<br /> +1 Reach: For one point of Mana, the spell's Duration is Lasting.<br /> <b>+2 Reach: The mage can scribe a Grimoire into the Anima Mundi. Such Grimoires manifest not as books and scrolls, but as vast constellations of stars or rock formations. Figuring out how to read one constitutes a Mystery unto itself.</b><br /> <br /> If you squint hard enough, its conceptually quite close.<br /> , <br /> Then i went a step further: would it be possible to scribe a Daimonomicon in the Anima mundi?<br /> From signs of sorcery<br /> Scribe Daimonomikon (Death, Fate, Mind, or Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 + Prime \u2022; or Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> <br /> I guess scribing the Daimonomicon in the Astral would be mind 3 + Prime 4, with a +2 reach to scribe it in the Anima mundi.<br /> <br /> What would the Mysterium think of a Legacy that passes on it's Attainments and Magical lore through the Anima mundi?<br /> I'm undecided on this: on the one hand it does preserve knowledge; on the other hand... anyone could get it.<br /> In hindsight, the Daimonomikon might not be such a great idea, given the Sympathy yantra thing though...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T16:37:12-08:00","id":1189309,"title":"","content":"Also straight up the biggest spell in Jonathan Strange and Mr Norrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/513-gatts","name":"Gatts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T17:22:06-08:00","id":1189315,"title":"","content":"Scribing a Daimonomkcon into the Anima Mundi would require at least Mind 4, not three, and probably Prime 1 or 4, with +2 Reach to pull it off. Other than that, seems correct. This might have an interesting interaction with the fact that if you're a Legacy Pedagogue you have a Connected Sympathetic connection with a constellation of stars or some other feature of the Anima Mundi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T17:37:11-08:00","id":1189320,"title":"","content":"It's risky business. It's no safer than anywhere else, it can't be moved, you could potentially be harmed sympathetically (or really, perhaps just pestered) using it, and it's out in the open or anyone (with the requisite knowledge and skill to find it) to learn from.<br /> <br /> That being said, it could propogate your Legacy quite effectively if you're lucky, and word spreads. Though given the relative scarcity of travellers that deep into the Astral, and the difficulty inherent in interpreting Anima Mundai phenomena, you might not get even one person who just stumbles across it.<br /> <br /> It's a much better idea to share your Legacy with another person first, then store an Astral Daimonomicon in the Temenos Realm of your Legacy you have forged.<br /> That way, even if every living member dies, someone could still use Time Magic to open up the Astral pathway to the lost Temenos realm, and find a Daimonomicon to rekindle it from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":".  Clarity 02-24-2018, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T21:25:03-08:00","id":1189342,"title":"","content":"Legacies are good, but I remember something about shaping the Temenos to create changes in humanity's culture and perceptions. I wonder if we'll get this &quot;Astral Shaping&quot; feat in upcoming supplements, because it sounds so promising. This Salinian Working may be an ambitious (and Obsessed) mage trying to wire better receptiveness to the Supernal in Sleepers, or at least create enough Sleepwalkers to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T02:26:14-08:00","id":1189371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1189230-the-salinian-working-in-mage-the-awakening-signs-of-sorcery-preview-materials?p=1189342#post1189342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Salinian Working may be an ambitious (and Obsessed) mage trying to wire better receptiveness to the Supernal in Sleepers, or at least create enough Sleepwalkers to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a Proximus lineage that is passed on through means other than inheritance?<br /> <br /> The legacy pedagogue combination did occur to me too; not sure about the implications of the connected sympathy though. Draws a way too large target on your back<br /> <br /> <br /> Something i found in the Shaping rituals thread in exalted forum:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=804494#post804494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But being an idealist, she wanted to be sure that those followed her path were at least decent people, not aspiring tyrants and warlords. So it was that her working included many trials intended to either eliminate or enlighten the unsuitable, and teaches shaping rituals based in the simple things Salina valued before all others: love, care, and respect for Creation and its inhabitants. You have followed the clues Salina and her students wove into Creation, and gained both insight and a measure of enlightenment along with sorcerous knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any thoughts on borrowing the mechanics for Keys and applying it to grimoires? i.e. Making a grimoire that can only be read if the reader meets a certain condition? Or requiring something like a quest, along the lines of Fate 4 Atonement.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... Fate 4, Mind 3, Prime 1, maybe. <br /> <br /> If an anima mundi rote is a Mystery, it would have an Opacity equal to dots in Highest arcana + 1 per extra conjunctional arcanum involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","user":"MovingMind","date":".  added Opacity bit at the end 02-25-2018, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T19:46:32-08:00","id":1190538,"title":"","content":"Given that all legacies represent a shared soul state as well as sorcerous knowledge, it's unavoidable that there be a realm associated with them in the Temenos. Whether or not it's well protected or reasonably navigable is a different question, but the fact is, the sympathy concern is part and parcel of being in a legacy. It's also a question whether such a realm would function as a Daimonomicon.<br /> <br /> Warding the daimonomicon should be possible, too, if mitigating that is a concern.<br /> <br /> Ed. One could decide that the Thyrsus watchtower was created by the Salinian working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 03-01-2018, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T22:13:01-08:00","id":1190569,"title":"","content":"I do not understand - is this official material, pointed by the devs to be in <b>Signs of Sorcery</b>? Or only original poster finding inspirational stuff in Exalted line?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T22:53:30-08:00","id":1190575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1189230-the-salinian-working-in-mage-the-awakening-signs-of-sorcery-preview-materials?p=1190569#post1190569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not understand - is this official material, pointed by the devs to be in <b>Signs of Sorcery</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9MmFicl9RQmJOZDA/view\" target=\"_blank\">This document</a>, from <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/grimoires-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">this open development post</a>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T23:49:10-08:00","id":1190580,"title":"","content":"Ninja'd; but yes, this is just me finding inspriation from Exalted, and combining it with Astral Grimoire from the Signs of Sorcery preview materials. <br /> <br /> I would like to make a legacy out of the Salinian school in exalted; or at least the &quot;drawing arcane knowledge from natural patterns&quot; part, but requiring a journey to the Temenos or Dreamtime in order to learn a Rote seems like a bit much; i guess it depends on how difficult you want it to be for a player to learn a rote.<br /> <br /> The closest i've come to something that fits the original material is the Fate 2 spell shifting the odds, which allows you to gain new Merits temporarily. However, it is intended for Social merits; while i would need it to grant the Grimoire merit.<br /> <br /> I'm currently debating whether that would be a fair use of the &quot;Atypical attainments&quot; rule, as something only members of the legacy can achieve.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T00:16:04-08:00","id":1190584,"title":"","content":"I remember the Sphinxes Legacy using Fate to pry out information from ambient patterns, although the information they gather is about solving puzzles. Maybe you could look them up?<br /> <br /> (I homebrewed them for 2E, but I used Prime for them IIRC. I\u2019m thinking of revisiting them and changing it back to Fate, after a small realization that Legacy Attainments don\u2019t have to always follow pre-existing spells so closely)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 03-01-2018, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T00:28:04-08:00","id":1190587,"title":"","content":"I've seen your work; Love it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This is what my first attainment is looking like: <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1 - Inspiration from nature</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Primary effect Fate 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Salinian develops a keen eye for the secret patterns of reality. The attainment emulates \u201cSerendipity\u201d, cast as an instant action, restricted to showing the mage interesting natural patterns. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Optional Prime 1 </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Studying the pattern takes one hour and mimics the spell \u201cDivination\u201d, with Reach expended for Detailed questions.</span></span><br /> <br /> Divination is a Time spell (obviously), but taken within the context of the Legacy, it's more interpreting a symbol to gain insight from it than asking about the future. So it's mechanically the same, but has a different context. It could also like the Dream merit, instead of mimicing the spell, but it's more of an academic difference.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T09:11:25-08:00","id":1190686,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">of her Imperial rites embedded arcane knowledge in the fabric of reality, as well as a simple enough path to follow for sleepers to awaken. Upon her Ascension, the Et voila, one legacy, for you to critique<br /> <br /> I think i put a bit too much functionality into the 3rd attainment; The 4th and 5th attainment probably could do with a bit of polishing too.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Salinians</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Salinian working</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The archmage Salina, as part of her Imperial rites embedded arcane knowledge in the fabric of reality, as well as a simple enough path to follow for sleepers to awaken. Upon her Ascension, the Exarchs erased most of her changes; The path to awaken sleepers has been erased, and the caches of knowledge have been obscured; all that remains is a Daimonomikon inscribed in the Dreaming earth. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Those who shape their souls following the teachings of the Daimonomikon gain access to the obscured caches of knowledge created by the omens of Salina\u2019s ascension.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Origins</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Parentage</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">: Obrimos, Free council</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Background</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">: The legacy\u2019s Daimonomikon is inscribed in the the Dreaming earth, and keyed to unlock itself only to aspiring mages that meet a certain level of decency. Since decent people are encountered in all walks of life, Salinians tend to have very varied backgrounds.However, they do tend to have unifying/defining behaviours, such as a keen eye for detail and an appreciation for the beauty of nature. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Appearance</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">: Due to the nature of the Legacy initiation, Salinians come from all walks of life; and they tend to look the part. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Doctrine</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Fate 2, Expression 2 and one of the following additional Skills at 2 dots or higher: Survival, Empathy, Animal Ken, Occult, or Science.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Initiation:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> The daimonomikon of the Salinians can be found in the Dreamtime. Due to Salina\u2019s idealism, the secrets of the Daimonomikon are only revealed to those that meet the requirements set by Salina herself, which basically can be summed up as \u201cBe a decent person\u201d. It is an unwritten rule in the legacy to not initialize members in any other way. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Organization:</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Due to the \u201copen source\u201d nature of the Salinian daimonomikon, Salinians don\u2019t really follow a formal hierarchy.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Theory: </span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">To those that know how to look, the fallen world contains a wealth of patterns, that when deciphered can reveal the secrets of reality.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Magic </span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Ruling Arcanum</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">: Fate</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Yantas</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">: Being within sensory rangin the presence of someone you share a Medium or Stronger sympathetic connection to (+1), Being in the of someone your True friend (and vice versa) (+2), Succeeding on an Expression relevant to the the spell (+2); verbally explaining the symbols of the yantras to someone close to you (+1); </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Oblations</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">: Spending quality time with someone you share a medium or stronger sympathetic connection. Tending to an aspect of creation or it\u2019s inhabitants. Teaching someone some knowledge you have gleaned from nature.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attainments</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First: Inspiration from nature</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Prerequisite: Initiation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Salinian develops a keen eye for the secret patterns of reality. The attainment emulates \u201cSerendipity\u201d, cast as an instant action, restricted to showing the mage interesting natural patterns. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Optional: Prime 1 </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Studying the pattern takes one hour and mimics the spell \u201cDivination\u201d, with Reach expended for Detailed questions.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second: Creation is your classroom</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Prerequisite: Fate 2, keen periphery</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">While studying a pattern, the Salinian sometimes glimpses actual supernal lore. This attainments emulates a modified version of \u201cShifting the Odds\u201d (reach to obtain results within one hour). The mage temporarily gains dots in the Grimoire merit equal to half of his prime dots. The Rotes contained in the \u201cgrimoire\u201d are subject to the following restrictions:</span></span><ul><li>They cannot already be known to the mage.</li> <li>The mage has to be able to cast the rote</li> <li>The number of highest arcanum in the rote cannot be higher than Mage's Fate Arcanum</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Optional: Prime 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The mage becomes a dab hand at observing the transient phenomena; mostly due to practice. This attainment mimics \u201cLight under a bushel\u201d, allowing the mage to make an extra number of rolls equal to Prime dots when scrutinizing a mystery. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Third: Grounding</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Prerequisite: Fate 3, One required skill raised to 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Sometimes, rather than a trove of supernal lore, sometimes, the insight provided by a pattern is more mundane, but no less useful. This attainment mimics \u201csuperlative luck\u201d (advanced), and usually manifests as a hunch at exactly the right moment.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Optional: Prime 3: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Salinian can enhance the natural patterns, highlighting the supernal significance of it. This manifests as one of two effects, either \u201cInvisible runes\u201d (Instant, Advanced duration) or \u201cScribe grimoire\u201d (Instant, Lasting, Key). The first effect can be used to create runes that can be used as per the normal Runes Yantra, in which case the runes are only visible to those with Mage sight, and resist being erased using a Clash of wills (gaining auto successes equal to prime dots). The secondary effect allows the mage to turn the symbols into a temporary grimoire; this lasts for the duration of the Invisible runes, and can only be read with Active mage sight.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fourth: Guidance</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Prerequisites: Fate 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The mage spends an hour studying a particular omen and gains the benefit of \u201cAtonement\u201d, cast with fate 4, with reach spent on allowing the quest to be completed by someone else. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Optional Prime 4: Building upon the previous attainment, Using Invisible runes as a yantra inscribed as a yantra benefits from \u201cAs above, so below\u201d, (8 again, Instant, Advanced duration).</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fifth: Synchronicity </span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Prerequisites: Fate 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Salinians with this level of attunement to the secrets of creation see reality in a fundamentally different way; the mage uses the changing portents to act and react almost precognitively. This mimics &quot;Exceptional luck&quot;, with reach expended on affecting spellcasting and reflexive activation. The mage can gain the benefit of resolving one of the following conditions every turn: Steadfast, Inspired, Informed, Charmed.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Optional: Prime 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">When witnessing a spell being cast, the supernal symbols are reflected in the omens the mage is so used to reading. This attainment mimics \u201cDisplay of Power\u201d, allowing the mage to gain rote action on counterspell rolls.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","user":"MovingMind","date":".  clarified 2nd attainment 03-02-2018, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11997-movingmind","name":"MovingMind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}